# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar Belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) is a variant of SKQD that replaces the need to choose an ansatz from which to sample bitstrings with an ensemble of time-evolution circuits constructed directly from the target Hamiltonian. This is achieved by subsampling smaller time-evolution operators from the Hamiltonian based on its coefficients, which is known as the qDRIFT Trotterization method.\n"
msgstr "[SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) ialah varian SKQD yang menggantikan keperluan untuk memilih ansatz yang darinya bitstring disampel dengan ensembel litar evolusi-masa yang dibina terus daripada Hamiltonian sasaran. Ini dicapai dengan subpensampelan operator evolusi-masa yang lebih kecil daripada Hamiltonian berdasarkan pekalinya, yang dikenali sebagai kaedah Trotterisasi qDRIFT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial makes use of [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to create the more natural fermionic circuits for the [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503) algorithm, followed by the use of fermionic layout and synthesis passes before plugging the circuits into the traditional Qiskit pipeline for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) untuk mencipta litar fermionik yang lebih semula jadi bagi algoritma [qDRIFT](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.070503), diikuti dengan penggunaan pass susun atur dan sintesis fermionik sebelum memasukkan litar ke dalam saluran paip Qiskit tradisional untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let the Hamiltonian be of the form:\n"
msgstr "Biarkan Hamiltonian dalam bentuk:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i h_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where, without loss of generality, we require $c_i > 0$ and that the largest eigenvalue of $h_i$ be equal, in absolute value, to $1$. Any signed or complex prefactor is absorbed into $h_i$, so the coefficients $c_i$ are strictly positive weights while the $h_i$ carry the direction of each term. Here $N$ is the number of terms (or, after grouping, the number of groups) in the Hamiltonian; it is a property of the Hamiltonian and is distinct from the number of operators sampled into a single circuit, written $n$ below.\n"
msgstr "di mana, tanpa kehilangan keumuman, kita memerlukan $c_i > 0$ dan nilai eigen terbesar bagi $h_i$ adalah sama, dalam nilai mutlak, dengan $1$. Sebarang faktor-awal bertanda atau kompleks diserap ke dalam $h_i$, jadi pekali $c_i$ ialah berat positif secara ketat manakala $h_i$ membawa arah setiap terma. Di sini $N$ ialah bilangan terma (atau, selepas pengumpulan, bilangan kumpulan) dalam Hamiltonian; ia ialah ciri Hamiltonian dan berbeza daripada bilangan operator yang disampel ke dalam satu litar, ditulis $n$ di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT algorithm then realizes, for the target time $t$, some operator $V_k$, where $k$ goes from $1 \\cdots K$ and signifies the $k_{th}$ SqDRIFT circuit, defined as:\n"
msgstr "Algoritma qDRIFT kemudian merealisasikan, bagi masa sasaran $t$, sesuatu operator $V_k$, di mana $k$ berjulat dari $1 \\cdots K$ dan menandakan litar SqDRIFT ke-$k$, ditakrifkan sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_k = \\prod_{j=1}^{n} e^{-i h_{k_j} \\lambda t / n }\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $n$ is the number of sampled operators per circuit and $K$ is the number of circuits in the ensemble. The product runs over the $n$ draws, not over all $N$ Hamiltonian terms, and because the terms are drawn with replacement, the same $h_i$ can appear more than once in a single $V_k$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini $n$ ialah bilangan operator yang disampel bagi setiap litar dan $K$ ialah bilangan litar dalam ensembel. Hasil darab berjalan merentas $n$ cabutan, bukan merentas kesemua $N$ terma Hamiltonian, dan kerana terma dicabut dengan penggantian, $h_i$ yang sama boleh muncul lebih daripada sekali dalam satu $V_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantity:\n"
msgstr "Kuantiti:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} c_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is the $L_1$ norm of the coefficients, so each of the $n$ steps evolves for the same duration $\\lambda t / n$ regardless of which term was drawn. The uniformity of the step angle is the characteristic feature of qDRIFT: a coefficient influences the result through *how often* its term is drawn, not through how far that term is rotated. The indices are sampled from the distribution:\n"
msgstr "ialah norma $L_1$ bagi pekali, jadi setiap satu daripada $n$ langkah berevolusi untuk tempoh yang sama $\\lambda t / n$ tanpa mengira terma mana yang dicabut. Keseragaman sudut langkah ialah ciri khusus qDRIFT: sesuatu pekali mempengaruhi hasil melalui *berapa kerap* termanya dicabut, bukan melalui berapa jauh terma itu diputar. Indeks disampel daripada taburan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P[k_i] = \\frac{c_i}{\\lambda}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the series $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ is a random sequence of term indices drawn from this distribution. Since the $c_i$ are positive and sum to $\\lambda$, this is a normalized probability distribution, and the expectation of the resulting channel over the random draws approximates evolution under $H$, with an error that decreases as $n$ grows. Note that the approximation error depends on $\\lambda$ rather than on the number of terms $N$.\n"
msgstr "jadi siri $(k_1, \\ldots, k_n)$ ialah jujukan rawak indeks terma yang dicabut daripada taburan ini. Kerana $c_i$ adalah positif dan berjumlah $\\lambda$, ini ialah taburan kebarangkalian ternormal, dan jangkaan saluran yang terhasil merentas cabutan rawak menghampiri evolusi di bawah $H$, dengan ralat yang berkurangan apabila $n$ bertambah. Perhatikan bahawa ralat penghampiran bergantung pada $\\lambda$ dan bukan pada bilangan terma $N$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The SqDRIFT paper writes the number of terms as $\\mathcal{N}$ and the sequence length as $N$; we use $N$ and $n$ here to keep the two clearly distinct.)\n"
msgstr "(Kertas SqDRIFT menulis bilangan terma sebagai $\\mathcal{N}$ dan panjang jujukan sebagai $N$; kami menggunakan $N$ dan $n$ di sini untuk mengekalkan kedua-duanya jelas berbeza.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to generate an ensemble of such randomized circuits. After we have created these circuits, similar to how we create a Krylov subspace for different operators, we sample bitstrings from multiple such operators with different time parameters. This ensures a higher overlap between the ground state vectors and sampled bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara menjana ensembel litar rawak sedemikian. Selepas kita mencipta litar ini, sama seperti kita mencipta subruang Krylov bagi operator yang berbeza, kita menyampel bitstring daripada beberapa operator sedemikian dengan parameter masa yang berbeza. Ini memastikan pertindihan yang lebih tinggi antara vektor keadaan dasar dan bitstring yang disampel.\n"

